  "name": "Fatty acid synthesis",
  "category": "metabolic",
  "topic": "metabolism",
  "summary": "In the fed state, excess acetyl-CoA is exported from mitochondria as citrate, converted to malonyl-CoA by acetyl-CoA carboxylase, and assembled into palmitate by fatty acid synthase — seven cycles of condensation, reduction, dehydration and reduction, powered by NADPH.",
  "evidence": "established",
  "layout": "chain",
  "location": "Cytosol (liver, adipose, lactating mammary gland)",
  "net": "8 Acetyl-CoA + 7 ATP + 14 NADPH + 14 H⁺ → Palmitate + 7 ADP + 7 Pᵢ + 14 NADP⁺ + 8 CoA + 6 H₂O",
  "clinical": "FASN is overexpressed in many cancers. ACC is inhibited by AMPK and by insulin-antagonising hormones; ACC inhibitors are being studied for NASH.",
